{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder\/batchlimit"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"]]},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Type Property","externalID":"s:21TelemetryDeckEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV10batchLimit12PropertyJSON0dG0VvpZ","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder.swift#L134","fileName":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder.swift"},"title":"batchLimit"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON\/BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The 100 events are what TelemetryDeck’s SwiftSDK sends in a request. The 333,333 bytes of an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event are a third of Ingest API v3’s limit: TelemetryDeck refuses a whole request when one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s JSON is over 1,000,000 bytes as its server writes it, which may be larger than the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder’s, and a third leaves room for the escapes a re-encoder commonly adds, such as "},{"code":"\\u","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and four hex digits for a character outside ASCII, and a space after each "},{"code":":","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":",","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"larger event is left out as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError\/oversized(byteCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck documents no limit on a request; its 1,000,000 bytes are the encoder’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bound, the most one event may be, which keeps a request to a size a retry can send again."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck’s limits on one request: 100 events and 1,000,000 bytes of body, and 333,333"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes of one event."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://PropertyJSON/documentation/PropertyJSON/BatchLimit":{"url":"\/documentation\/propertyjson\/batchlimit","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchLimit"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchLimit"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The most an ingestion endpoint takes in one request: how many records, how many bytes of body,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","